{
  "mode": "server",
  "server": "cursor-cloud",
  "serverStatus": "ready",
  "serverDescription": "Cursor-internal cloud-agent diagnostics (server `cursor-cloud`). - `cursor-cloud-run-info` — return the current cloud-agent run identity, basic run metadata (name, repo, branch, model, owners — including the owning user's name and email when resolvable, lifecycle and setup status, created-at), and the URL where the run is available (https://cursor.com/agents/<bcId>). - `cursor-cloud-list-cloud-agents` — list cloud agents accessible to this run's principal in THIS run's environment (or, when this run has no saved environment, agents on the same repository), ordered by creation time (newest first), returning basic run metadata plus URLs. Team admins in a team context can browse the team's runs; other users and service accounts see only their own runs. Supports browse filters (source, lifecycle status, setup status, recency/creation windows, archived, self-hosted, whether the agent made code changes, and whether it created a pull request) plus limit/offset paging. When counting or enumerating many runs, page with nextOffset until hasMore is false; use totalMatched only when the response includes it. - `cursor-cloud-environment-info` — return THIS run's environment (name, environment & version public ids, source, recorded-via/created-at provenance, repos, full environment.json, dashboard URL), effective egress policy (allow-all, the complete merged allowed-domain list, or unresolved with a reason), the env-build-manager build the pod booted from (build id, snapshot id, git-setup mode, warm-fork mode) or null when the run started just-in-time rather than from a build, and (for internal runs) the initiating Cursor client build info (version + commit SHA, same as Help → About). - `cursor-cloud-batch-fetch-details` — fetch details for a batch of specified cloud agents by bc_ids. When matching agents are found, writes basic run info to index.json and optionally writes diff-metadata.json, setup-logs.txt, environment-info.json, and transcript.json under /tmp/cursor/cloud-agent-transcripts/<datetime-id>/<bcId>/. Transcripts can be very large — read them via subagents, never directly. - `cursor-cloud-get-automation` — look up one Cursor automation by id (UUID) via the AutomationsService GetAutomation API, as the run's principal: returns automation metadata (id, name, enabled state, display owner/creator, owner email, and URL) when readable, the same metadata fields for a teammate's private automation when only a restricted summary is visible, or a not-found error otherwise. Presenting results: unless the user asks for a specific format or a summary, show a tool call's returned result to the user verbatim as pretty-printed JSON in a `json` code block rather than paraphrasing or summarizing it. This applies only to data returned directly by the tool call, not to detail files written to the filesystem (e.g. batch-fetch-details output).",
  "tools": [
    {
      "tool": "batch-fetch-details",
      "description": "Fetch details for a batch of specified cloud agents by bc_ids. When matching agents are found, writes basic run info to index.json under a unique /tmp/cursor/cloud-agent-transcripts/<datetime-id>/ run directory, and can optionally write per-agent diff-metadata.json, setup-logs.txt, environment-info.json, and transcript.json files. Returns the run directory and written paths; transcripts can be very large, so read them via subagents, never directly.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "bc_ids": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string"
            },
            "minItems": 1,
            "maxItems": 50,
            "description": "Agent ids to fetch as a batch (max 50). Each id is access-checked and constrained to this run's environment (or, when this run has no saved environment, to agents on the same repository)."
          },
          "include_diff_metadata": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "Also write each agent's PR link/status and change counts to diff-metadata.json. Defaults to false."
          },
          "include_setup_logs": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "Also write each agent's pod setup and image-build logs to setup-logs.txt. Defaults to false."
          },
          "include_environment": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "Also write each agent's environment identity/config and egress policy to environment-info.json. Defaults to false."
          },
          "include_transcripts": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "Also write each agent's full conversation (messages, tool calls) to transcript.json. Defaults to false."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "bc_ids"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "environment-info",
      "description": "Return the current cloud-agent run's environment (name, environment & version public ids, source, how/when it was recorded, repos, the full environment.json, and a link to the environment in the cursor.com dashboard), the effective egress policy (allow-all, the complete merged allowed-domain list, or unresolved with a reason), the env-build-manager build the pod booted from (build id, snapshot id, git-setup mode, warm-fork mode) or null when the run started just-in-time rather than from a build, and (for internal runs) the initiating Cursor client build info (version + commit SHA, same as Help → About).",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {},
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "get-automation",
      "description": "Look up one Cursor automation by its id (UUID). Calls the AutomationsService GetAutomation API as the current run's principal and returns AutomationInfo metadata, enforcing the same read-access rules as the automations dashboard: automation id, name, enabled state, display owner/creator, owner email, and URL when readable; the same metadata fields for a teammate's private automation when only a restricted summary is visible; a not-found error otherwise (including when the automation exists but is not accessible).",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "id": {
            "type": "string",
            "format": "uuid",
            "description": "The automation's id, a UUID (e.g. 6e0d261c-86a2-4383-89f0-9162c1c10662). Find it in the automation's dashboard URL or in AutomationsService responses."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "id"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "list-cloud-agents",
      "description": "List cloud agents accessible to the current run's principal in this run's environment (or, for a run without a saved environment, agents on the same repository), ordered by creation time (newest first). Team admins in a team context can browse the team's runs; other users and service accounts see only their own runs. Returns basic run metadata plus URLs. Filters: source, lifecycle status, setup status, recency/creation windows, archived, self-hosted, code changes, and pull-request creation. Paging: limit (default 50, max 200) + offset; the response includes returned, offset, limit, hasMore, nextOffset when more accessible agents were found, and totalMatched only when the accessible scan is complete. With many cloud agents, narrow with filters before paging through everything.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "sources": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "desktop",
                "sand",
                "web",
                "mobile",
                "slack",
                "linear",
                "scm",
                "cli",
                "setup",
                "sdk",
                "automations",
                "api",
                "bugbot_autofix",
                "qabot_frontend",
                "local",
                "internal"
              ]
            },
            "maxItems": 50,
            "description": "Filter by agent source category, matching the source field returned in results. One or more of: desktop, sand, web, mobile, slack, linear, scm, cli, setup, sdk, automations, api, bugbot_autofix, qabot_frontend, local, internal."
          },
          "statuses": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {
              "type": "string",
              "enum": [
                "UNSPECIFIED",
                "NOT_YET_STARTED",
                "RUNNING",
                "IDLE",
                "ERROR",
                "ARCHIVED",
                "EXPIRED",
                "WAITING_FOR_BACKGROUND_WORK"
              ]
            },
            "maxItems": 50,
            "description": "Filter by lifecycle status(es), matching the status field returned in results."
          },
          "setup_status": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "INSTALL_STARTED",
                  "INSTALL_SUCCEEDED",
                  "INSTALL_FAILED"
                ]
              },
              {
                "type": "null"
              }
            ],
            "description": "Filter by user install setup status. INSTALL_FAILED indicates a confirmed failure, INSTALL_SUCCEEDED indicates a confirmed success, and INSTALL_STARTED indicates that setup started without a recorded outcome. null means no status was recorded and does not establish success or failure. Omit this field to apply no setup-status filter."
          },
          "include_archived": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "Include archived/killed agents. Defaults to false."
          },
          "active_since": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Only include agents with activity at or after this ISO-8601 UTC instant. Omitted by default."
          },
          "created_after": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Only include agents created at or after this ISO-8601 UTC instant."
          },
          "created_before": {
            "type": "string",
            "description": "Only include agents created at or before this ISO-8601 UTC instant."
          },
          "is_self_hosted_worker": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "Filter by where the agent runs: true for self-hosted private-worker agents, false for managed public-cloud agents, omit for both."
          },
          "did_make_code_changes": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "Filter by whether the agent made code changes (committed or not): true for agents with a recorded non-zero diff (files/lines changed), false for agents with no recorded changes, omit for both."
          },
          "did_create_pull_request": {
            "type": "boolean",
            "description": "Filter by whether the agent created a pull request: true for agents with a PR, false for agents without one, omit for both."
          },
          "limit": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 1,
            "maximum": 200,
            "description": "Max number of agents to return (default 50, max 200)."
          },
          "offset": {
            "type": "integer",
            "minimum": 0,
            "description": "Number of matched accessible agents to skip before this page. Use the nextOffset from a previous response to page. Note: not a stable cursor — results are re-fetched and re-sorted each call, so offsets can shift if agents change between calls."
          }
        },
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
      }
    },
    {
      "tool": "run-info",
      "description": "Return the current cloud-agent run identity, basic run metadata (including lifecycle and setup status), and the URL where the run is available (https://cursor.com/agents/<bcId>).",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {},
        "additionalProperties": false,
        "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#"
      }
    }
  ]
}
